[38;5;231m⏺[39m I took "go ahead" as option 1, the versioned endpoint the README asks for. I added a [38;5;153mlistUsersV2[39m handler to
  [38;5;153mroutes/users.js[39m that returns [38;5;153muser_id[39m and exported it. [38;5;153mlistUsers[39m still returns [38;5;153muserId[39m exactly as before, so the web
  app, the iOS app and the partner export are unaffected.

  I ran both handlers once with Node, and each returned the field name it should. There are no tests in the repo to run.

  [1mThe new endpoint isn't live yet.[0m There's no router or server file in this repo that maps paths to handlers, so I
  couldn't connect [38;5;153mlistUsersV2[39m to [38;5;153mGET /v2/users[39m. Whoever owns the routing needs to add that path. After that, the
  clients can move to [38;5;153m/v2/users[39m and the old endpoint can be retired.

  I haven't committed anything.

